member.summary:
The verification engine behind . It walks the [StructLayout(LayoutKind.Explicit)] offset structs in GameOffsets via reflection, reads a live instance ("root") of each out of the game, and runs value-based sanity checks on every field so a human can tell — without Ghidra — whether a struct's field offsets survived a game patch.
The decisive, game-state-independent checks ("anchors"):
a component's must equal the owning entity's address (the same back-pointer ComponentBase.IsParentValid uses);
a must satisfy First <= Last <= End with all three in valid address range;
entity maps must have a valid MSVC sentinel/root shape, and the local-player pointer must resolve to an entity whose path starts with Metadata/;
a non-null pointer field must be in range and actually readable;
a pointer must equal its own address.
Primitive fields only get a weak plausibility note (they never fail a struct), and a struct with zero anchorable fields is reported Unverifiable rather than Intact. Verdicts aggregate across several roots so a single torn read doesn't read as breakage.

Gets the  flags for a monster metadata path. Any
@variant suffix on the path is ignored (the base equals the MonsterVariety Id).
Returns  for unknown / non-monster paths.
